[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector","page":"API Reference","text":"DirectionVector{FT<:AbstractFloat} <: FieldVector{3,FT}\nDirectionVector(x::FT, y::FT, z::FT) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nUnit-length vector representing direction in 3D space.\n\nConstructor arguments\n\nx, y, z: direction components [-]\n\nFields\n\nxd, yd, zd: normalised direction components [-]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector-Union{Tuple{FT}, Tuple{FT, FT}} where FT<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"DirectionVector(alpha::FT, beta::FT) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nConstructor for DirectionVector using spherical coordinates.\n\nArguments\n\nalpha: elevation angle [radians]\nbeta: azimuth angle [radians]\n\nReturns\n\nDirectionVector{FT} constructed from spherical coordinates\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.PositionVector","page":"API Reference","text":"PositionVector{FT<:AbstractFloat} <: FieldVector{3,FT}\nPositionVector(xc::FT, yc::FT, zc::FT) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nVector representing position in 3D space.\n\nConstructor arguments\n\nxc, yc, zc: position components [metres]\n\nFields\n\nSame as constructor arguments\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.PositionVector"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.t_at_plane-Union{Tuple{FT}, Tuple{RayTracingBasics.PositionVector{FT}, RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector{FT}, Int64, FT}} where FT<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"t_at_plane(ray_origin::PositionVector{FT}, ray_direction::DirectionVector{FT}, axis::Int, c::FT) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCompute the ray parameter t at which a ray intersects an axis-aligned plane.\n\nArguments\n\nray_origin, ray_direction: ray origin [metres] and direction [-]\naxis: axis normal to the plane (1=x, 2=y, 3=z)\nc: coordinate of the plane along axis [metres]\n\nReturns\n\nFT: ray parameter t at the intersection point [metres]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.t_at_plane"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.to_homogeneous-Union{Tuple{RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector{FT}}, Tuple{FT}} where FT<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"to_homogeneous(v::DirectionVector{FT}) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nConvert a DirectionVector to homogeneous coordinates by appending a zero weight.\n\nArguments\n\nv: direction vector in 3D space\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{4, FT}: homogeneous coordinate vector [xd, yd, zd, 0]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.to_homogeneous"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#RayTracingBasics.to_homogeneous-Union{Tuple{RayTracingBasics.PositionVector{FT}}, Tuple{FT}} where FT<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"to_homogeneous(v::PositionVector{FT}) where {FT<:AbstractFloat}\n\nConvert a PositionVector to homogeneous coordinates by appending a unit weight.\n\nArguments\n\nv: position vector in 3D space\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{4, FT}: homogeneous coordinate vector [xc, yc, zc, 1]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RayTracingBasics.to_homogeneous"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StaticArraysCore.similar_type-Union{Tuple{S}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{<:RayTracingBasics.DirectionVector}, Type{T}, StaticArraysCore.Size{S}}} where {T, S}","page":"API Reference","text":"StaticArrays.similar_type(::Type{<:DirectionVector}, ::Type{T}, s::Size{S}) where {T,S}\n\nExtend StaticArrays.similar_type to return a standard SVector when doing maths on a DirectionVector. This is because the result of arithmetic on a DirectionVector is not generally a unit vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StaticArraysCore.similar_type"},{"category":"section","location":"#RayTracingBasics.jl","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for RayTracingBasics.","title":"RayTracingBasics.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"RayTracingBasics\")","title":"Installation"}]
